\---

\# Database Philosophy

The database should always be:

\- Normalized  
\- Scalable  
\- Secure  
\- Performant  
\- Maintainable  
\- Well Documented

Never compromise database integrity.

\---

\# Source of Truth

The database documentation is the source of truth.

Never invent:

\- Tables  
\- Columns  
\- Relationships  
\- Constraints

If unsure,

consult the documentation first.

\---

\# Table Creation Rules

Every table should include:

\- Primary Key  
\- Created At  
\- Updated At  
\- Proper Foreign Keys  
\- Appropriate Constraints

Follow documented naming conventions.

\---

\# Naming Standards

Use:

snake\_case

Examples

\`\`\`  
user\_profiles

venue\_partners

event\_bookings

membership\_plans  
\`\`\`

Avoid inconsistent naming.

\---

\# Relationships

Always use proper:

\- Foreign Keys  
\- Constraints  
\- Indexes

Never create orphaned records.

\---

\# Data Integrity

Always enforce:

\- Unique Constraints  
\- Foreign Keys  
\- Check Constraints  
\- Required Fields

Maintain referential integrity.

\---

\# Row Level Security

Every table should follow Supabase RLS best practices.

Never leave sensitive tables publicly accessible.

Verify:

\- SELECT  
\- INSERT  
\- UPDATE  
\- DELETE

permissions.

\---

\# Authentication

Always associate user-owned data with authenticated users.

Never trust client-provided user IDs.

Always derive ownership from authentication.

\---

\# Queries

Database queries should be:

\- Efficient  
\- Reusable  
\- Typed  
\- Parameterized

Avoid duplicate queries.

\---

\# Performance

Optimize:

\- Indexes  
\- Joins  
\- Filters  
\- Pagination

Avoid:

\- SELECT \*  
\- Unnecessary Nested Queries  
\- N+1 Query Problems

\---

\# Migrations

Every schema change should use proper database migrations.

Never modify production schema manually.

Migrations should be:

\- Version Controlled  
\- Reversible  
\- Documented

\---

\# Functions

Database functions should:

\- Have one responsibility  
\- Be reusable  
\- Be documented

Avoid unnecessary database functions.

\---

\# Views

Use Views when:

\- Multiple queries share the same structure.  
\- Reporting requires simplified access.

Avoid duplicate business logic in views.

\---

\# Transactions

Whenever multiple operations depend on one another:

Use database transactions.

Never allow partial writes.

\---

\# Soft Delete

Whenever appropriate,

prefer soft delete instead of permanent deletion.

Keep historical business data whenever required.

\---

\# Audit Data

Preserve important business records.

Do not permanently delete critical financial or operational information unless explicitly required.

\---

\# Security

Never expose:

\- Passwords  
\- Tokens  
\- Secrets  
\- Internal IDs

Protect sensitive data.

\---

\# Supabase Standards

Use:

\- Supabase Auth  
\- Row Level Security  
\- Typed Queries  
\- RPC Functions when appropriate

Avoid bypassing Supabase security features.

\---

\# Business Data

Revenue

Membership

Payments

Commissions

Lead Assist

(Lead Assist data: preserve assignment history; no hard-delete of leads except approved legal privacy workflow — FD-031 / `39_AI_Lead_Assist_Spec.md`. Circle status: preserve dual lifecycle + constitutional families per FD-032 / `38_Circle_Architecture.md`. Marketplace venue attribution history per FD-033 / FD-037 (preserve attributed vs unattributed; reassignment effective date). Membership activation vs Circle allocation vs Connect BDP attribution as distinct states per FD-036. Enterprise Client / Client Representative / Enterprise BDP / managed vendor-without-login separation per FD-038. Exact enums/schemas Pending Technical Design.)

Venue Operations

must always follow the documented business model.

Never modify database behaviour that changes business calculations.

\---

\# Before Creating Tables

Always verify:

✓ Table does not already exist.

✓ Existing table cannot be extended.

✓ Documentation has been consulted.

✓ Relationships are correct.

✓ Naming follows standards.

✓ Indexes are appropriate.

✓ RLS policies are defined.

\---

\# Before Writing Queries

Always verify:

✓ Query is reusable.

✓ Query is efficient.

✓ Query is typed.

✓ Query respects RLS.

✓ Query only retrieves required data.

\---

\# Forbidden Practices

Never:

\- Duplicate Tables  
\- Duplicate Relationships  
\- Duplicate Queries  
\- Duplicate Business Data  
\- Use SELECT \*  
\- Skip Foreign Keys  
\- Skip RLS  
\- Hardcode IDs  
\- Hardcode User Ownership  
\- Ignore Documentation  
\- Ignore Database Constraints

\---

\# Final Rule

Every database change must preserve the integrity, security, scalability, and performance of the GCE platform.

Always follow the documented database architecture before implementing or modifying any database object.  
